Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.60,0:00:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.42,0:00:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,This girl is Jolyne Kujo, but where\Nin God's name is Lang Wrangler?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.36,0:00:23.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Am I right to assume that\Nhe failed his objective
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.88,0:00:26.16,Default,,0,0,0,,and she still has the\Ndisc in her possession?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.24,0:00:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,If so, within a few moments,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.92,0:00:31.06,Default,,0,0,0,,she will meet someone at the courtyard\Nand hand the disc off to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.14,0:00:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I know that guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.50,0:00:35.15,Default,,0,0,0,,He serves as a priest\Nat the prison's chapel.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.68,0:00:37.12,Default,,0,0,0,,What is he doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.86,0:00:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Did she find out?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.92,0:00:40.75,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.83,0:00:42.43,Default,,0,0,0,,If she had any inkling\Nthat I was her enemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.52,0:00:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,,we would be in the midst\Nof battle right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.42,0:00:46.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on! Father, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.36,0:00:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I beg of you, whatever you do,\Nplease don't sound that alarm!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.94,0:00:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The last thing that I want here is to\Ncause trouble or make some kind of scene!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.52,0:00:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,What do I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.80,0:00:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Should I take the chance\Nand knock him out?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.00,0:01:02.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure I could, if it's to\Nbring my old man back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.12,0:01:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Hitting a priest is nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.48,0:01:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Aren't you ignoring the\Nreal problem happening here?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.42,0:01:13.52,Default,,0,0,0,,You've taken someone else's work permit\Ncard and used it to get me to open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.60,0:01:17.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Pray tell what has become of the\Nprisoner this card actually belongs to,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.70,0:01:18.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Lang Wrangler.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.20,0:01:23.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you just met me, so I won't\Nask you to believe what I'm saying.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.52,0:01:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,But I have no reason\Nto lie to you, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.82,0:01:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I was assaulted by the prisoner you're\Nreferring to, so I defended myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.60,0:01:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,He's in that hamper probably dreaming\Nabout how I knocked him out cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.46,0:01:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Regardless of the reason, I am obligated\Nto report this matter to the authorities.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.86,0:01:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure, do what you have to.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.76,0:01:43.76,Default,,0,0,0,,However, it has to be after\NI get to the courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.96,0:01:45.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me two minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.38,0:01:47.82,Default,,0,0,0,,No, all I need is a single\Nsolitary minute, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.90,0:01:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me go to the courtyard\Nand you can turn me in.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.38,0:01:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That's all I ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.78,0:01:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you asking me to\Noverlook your wrongdoings?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.32,0:01:58.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone's life is on the line.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.94,0:02:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,My own dad's life and spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.50,0:02:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Surely a priest like yourself\Ncan understand my situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.68,0:02:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you by your lonesome?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.46,0:02:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Or is there anyone else in here with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.00,0:02:10.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Nuh-uh.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.92,0:02:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,It's only me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.64,0:02:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe I just lied to a priest.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.30,0:02:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,But a tiny lie like that can be forgiven.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.90,0:02:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,and mentioning the disks would\Nsend up immediate red flags.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.02,0:02:24.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Father, one minute is all I ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.78,0:02:27.74,Default,,0,0,0,,In most cases, when someone\Ndoes something for others,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.82,0:02:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,they expect to receive some\Nsort of reward in return.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.20,0:02:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,To be kind to others is to expect that\Nsame kindness from those you give it to,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.98,0:02:38.62,Default,,0,0,0,,and that cannot be called\Nunconditional love.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.70,0:02:40.64,Default,,0,0,0,,True unconditional love, my dear,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.04,0:02:44.39,Default,,0,0,0,,is the reward of eventually\Nreaching the gates of heaven.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.82,0:02:45.76,Default,,0,0,0,,You may go.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.84,0:02:48.96,Default,,0,0,0,,So, I will pretend that our\Npaths never crossed here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.40,0:02:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,But per your request,\Nyou only have one minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.42,0:02:57.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I trust you'll return to this gate\Nby then and not a second longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.20,0:03:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I had to let her go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.16,0:03:05.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Despite her lie, I know\Nsomeone is hiding there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.42,0:03:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,If she does have comrades around,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.28,0:03:11.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I cannot risk revealing\Nthat I am Palesnake's user,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.12,0:03:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,even if it is to dispose of Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.48,0:03:26.68,Default,,0,0,0,,According to the Speedwagon Foundation,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.76,0:03:30.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll know how to hand over the disc\Nonce I arrive at the courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.06,0:03:32.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess this is what they meant.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.88,0:03:37.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.79,0:03:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you have a pass that\Npermits you to be out here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.16,0:03:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna say that's a no.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.32,0:03:52.79,Default,,0,0,0,,So that must mean you're trying to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.98,0:03:53.81,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.89,0:03:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.78,0:03:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounding the alarm was\Nnever part of my plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.02,0:04:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad I thought ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.06,0:04:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Having a guard patrol the\Ncourtyard was the perfect decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.56,0:04:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.84,0:04:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Fight!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.88,0:04:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Mode Nash no survival day. Get away!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.02,0:04:53.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't wanna see!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.20,0:04:56.42,Default,,0,0,0,,No time! Let's get started! Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.68,0:04:59.28,Default,,0,0,0,,1, 2, 3. Coming right away!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.46,0:05:01.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm on me! I'm on me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.42,0:05:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm on me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.86,0:05:06.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.00,0:05:09.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Break out! Tick up! I'm on me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.50,0:05:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm on me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.32,0:05:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Break out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.88,0:05:15.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Break out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.86,0:05:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't stop beating!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.62,0:05:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't stop beating!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.88,0:05:31.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't stop beating! I'm mad!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.08,0:05:48.48,Default,,0,0,0,,In the year 1988, my\Nlife took a turn. I met a
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.56,0:05:50.94,Default,,0,0,0,,man from Egypt who possessed\Nthe ability to stop
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.02,0:05:53.74,Default,,0,0,0,,time itself and we\Ndeveloped a rather close
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.82,0:05:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,relationship one evening\Nhe suddenly told me this
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.58,0:06:02.32,Default,,0,0,0,,If someone wished to go to\Nheaven, there may be a way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.74,0:06:05.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He was young and unbelievably beautiful,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.68,0:06:09.44,Default,,0,0,0,,but with an aura about him that suggested\Nhe had lived for hundreds of years.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.52,0:06:13.62,Default,,0,0,0,,At that time, I was 16 and a student\Naspiring to go to a seminary.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.48,0:06:17.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, don't look at me that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.72,0:06:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just talking about the human mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.96,0:06:22.34,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not like I'm telling\Nyou to wither and die.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.42,0:06:26.08,Default,,0,0,0,,This heaven pertains to our spirits\Nand where they go after death.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.16,0:06:26.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.07,0:06:29.12,Default,,0,0,0,,As your spirit evolves,\Nso too does your power.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.36,0:06:31.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Where they ultimately end up is
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.58,0:06:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,what fascinates me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.60,0:06:36.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Surely you of all people\Nunderstand what I'm talking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.90,0:06:39.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It's there that one will\Nfind true happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.96,0:06:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,That is, if they can make\Nit into heaven, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.12,0:06:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Though I'm aware, joy cannot be\Nfound by having an invincible body,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.44,0:06:48.30,Default,,0,0,0,,vast riches,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.52,0:06:54.74,Default,,0,0,0,,or even reigning over all humanity\Nin the end the true winner is the one
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.82,0:07:00.06,Default,,0,0,0,,who gets to witness heaven that's why\NI will get there someday no matter what
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.14,0:07:06.60,Default,,0,0,0,,it costs me and how are you going to\Nachieve that exactly ah well I wrote
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.68,0:07:13.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The process in a notebook one day find\Nme in Egypt. I'll show it to you there.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.04,0:07:18.56,Default,,0,0,0,,If I ever hope to figure this\Nout, I will need you to assist me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.56,0:07:23.09,Default,,0,0,0,,However, before I could learn\Nthe means of attaining Heaven,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.94,0:07:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,the notebook he spoke of was burned to ash\Nby none other than Jolene Kujo's father,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.28,0:07:35.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro Kujo.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.32,0:07:39.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro laid eyes on the contents\Nof the notebook that day,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.66,0:07:43.66,Default,,0,0,0,,and with the book gone, the information\Nwas sealed with him forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.66,0:07:48.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Along with the man who aimed\Nfor heaven, Dio Brando himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.92,0:07:56.34,Default,,0,0,0,,For the next 20 years, I waited patiently\Nfor my chance to obtain Jotaro's memories,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.66,0:08:00.19,Default,,0,0,0,,so that I could relive the\Nmoment that he read the notebook.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.54,0:08:04.28,Default,,0,0,0,,And finally, after decades, I got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.48,0:08:10.04,Default,,0,0,0,,His memories were mine, along with the stand\Nthat surpassed even Dio, Star Platinum.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.12,0:08:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I ensured that Jotaro's\Nbody would wither and decay.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.34,0:08:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And although his troublesome daughter\Nbehaved in ways I never could have expected,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.08,0:08:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,it's all taken care of now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.22,0:08:27.05,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.13,0:08:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,She got shot?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.32,0:08:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene got shot? But by who? A guard?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.06,0:08:34.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Or maybe that bastard Pale\NSnake figured out where she was
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.96,0:08:38.73,Default,,0,0,0,,going to deliver the disc and\Nhe's hiding around here somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.12,0:08:42.95,Default,,0,0,0,,JOLENE!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.84,0:08:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,The Guard and Control will take\Ncare of retrieving Star Platinum,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.22,0:08:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,so there's no reason for\Nme to stay here anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.02,0:08:56.49,Default,,0,0,0,,With that out of the way, I\Nshould head back to the chapel.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.04,0:08:58.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Hm?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.95,0:09:00.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What was I doing out here again?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.34,0:09:02.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh right, the disc.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.72,0:09:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I was given orders to bring this\Nthing back without a scratch on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.52,0:09:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,And I was also ordered to make sure\NJolene Cujoh was finished off for good.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.34,0:09:15.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Thing is, I don't know\Nwho gave me these orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.52,0:09:18.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't seem to remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.42,0:09:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Doesn't matter. Either way,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.60,0:09:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I was given orders to completely blast\Nstraight through Jolene's head with this gun.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.94,0:09:33.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.98,0:09:37.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, there's nothing I\Ncan do to help you now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.16,0:09:41.28,Default,,0,0,0,,In your greatest moment of\Nneed, I'm utterly useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.58,0:09:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,It's over now, Jolene Kujo!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.28,0:10:03.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.08,0:10:09.04,Default,,0,0,0,,My weather forecast is a\Npower to control the weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.78,0:10:12.28,Default,,0,0,0,,At this point, this is all I can offer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.92,0:10:19.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene, I wasn't able to save you, but\NI might be able to protect the disk.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.20,0:10:24.40,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you still have the strength\Nwithin you to keep fighting,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.82,0:10:27.46,Default,,0,0,0,,you may be able to survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.12,0:10:37.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Between the years of 1887 and 1974 in the
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.68,0:10:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,state of Florida alone\Nthere were more than
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.24,0:10:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,50 reported cases of fish frogs snakes and
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.00,0:10:46.56,Default,,0,0,0,,sheep falling from the sky in unbelievable
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.64,0:10:52.72,Default,,0,0,0,,numbers it was caused by a tornado at least\Nthat's what they say and these colorful
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.80,0:10:57.62,Default,,0,0,0,,amphibians are poison dart frogs that live\Non treetops in Central and South America.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.70,0:11:00.48,Default,,0,0,0,,They carry a deadly poison\Nunder their skin that
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.56,0:11:03.26,Default,,0,0,0,,aboriginal Americans\Nused for their blowguns.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.48,0:11:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,What the actual fuck is going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.64,0:11:22.36,Default,,0,0,0,,This is judging by the\Ncolor of these frogs' skin.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.54,0:11:24.40,Default,,0,0,0,,They're most certainly poison dart frogs.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.48,0:11:28.08,Default,,0,0,0,,It takes less than a few seconds for\Nthe poison to get inside the body,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.16,0:11:30.72,Default,,0,0,0,,causing the heart and\Nrespiratory system to stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.80,0:11:35.33,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the bodily fluid that's being\Nsplattered all over the place right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.04,0:11:36.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Halesnake!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.24,0:11:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,But this power, could it be his\Nability to control the weather?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.38,0:11:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather forecast.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.96,0:11:46.20,Default,,0,0,0,,He's supposed to have lost his memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.80,0:11:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Was he the one hiding behind the oil drum?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.56,0:11:51.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I must go.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.98,0:11:53.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the card key?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.48,0:12:25.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Not good.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.68,0:12:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The frog's fluid is\Nsoaking into my thread.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.86,0:12:29.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.77,0:12:31.89,Default,,0,0,0,,If somebody can hear me, open the gate!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.98,0:12:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.52,0:12:35.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.00,0:12:37.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Maintain your peace of mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.18,0:12:40.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What should I do at a time like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.86,0:12:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Two. Three. Five.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.86,0:12:44.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I must stay calm.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.24,0:12:47.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Count prime numbers to\Ncompose my thoughts.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.24,0:12:52.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Prime numbers are lonely numbers that can\Nonly be divided by one and themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.78,0:12:56.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It gives me courage. 23
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.76,0:13:01.70,Default,,0,0,0,,28 no it's 29 damn it
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.78,0:13:04.92,Default,,0,0,0,,the filthy frogs are\Nclean to my 800 pants?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.58,0:13:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather forecast is at\Nthe laundry room he's too
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.64,0:13:12.14,Default,,0,0,0,,far I can't make him stop\Nthese frogs from Raining
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.22,0:13:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,down escape is my only\Nviable option 41 yes
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.78,0:13:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,that's right the guard\Nthat was at the Courtyard?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.26,0:13:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to him?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.44,0:13:23.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Is he still under my control? Hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.92,0:13:24.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.96,0:13:26.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Guard, are you there?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.28,0:13:27.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Get back in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.66,0:13:29.14,Default,,0,0,0,,That is a direct order!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.94,0:13:36.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I need your help, Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.68,0:13:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Please help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.26,0:13:41.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Please beg God to spare\Nmy soul from this hell!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.96,0:13:46.78,Default,,0,0,0,,43, 47, 53, 59.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.06,0:13:48.26,Default,,0,0,0,,The Poison One.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.34,0:13:49.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm begging you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.16,0:13:52.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell the Lord to save me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.74,0:13:54.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Stay calm and listen to my voice!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.64,0:13:55.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I need your card key!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.12,0:13:57.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Get over here and give it to me quickly!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.86,0:14:01.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Could I be saved if I give this to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.26,0:14:03.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.17,0:14:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't take it out while you're over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.68,0:14:05.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.96,0:14:16.08,Default,,0,0,0,,67... 71...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.84,0:14:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,What on earth is going on in this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.92,0:14:21.08,Default,,0,0,0,,All those frogs?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.86,0:14:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what a relief.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.66,0:14:25.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, sir, I need you to\Nopen this gate immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.00,0:14:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, why are you here, Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.92,0:14:28.76,Default,,0,0,0,,What's happening?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.84,0:14:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.96,0:14:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,A tornado, maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.06,0:14:32.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Now please, just hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.94,0:14:34.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand. Right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.54,0:14:38.88,Default,,0,0,0,,These frogs are...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.96,0:14:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you standing there for?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.80,0:14:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We have another guard in\Nhere who's already fallen.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.00,0:14:44.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to open the gate!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.22,0:14:46.36,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't mean he's...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.88,0:14:48.74,Default,,0,0,0,,For now, try to remain calm, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.82,0:14:51.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll go find someone\Nwho can help right away!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.26,0:14:52.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.17,0:14:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Where do you think you're going?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.48,0:14:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,All you have to do is hit the switch\Nover here and the gate will open!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.12,0:14:58.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I understand that, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.06,0:15:00.77,Default,,0,0,0,,But there may be a liability.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.88,0:15:02.94,Default,,0,0,0,,So, I need to check with my supervisor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.02,0:15:04.94,Default,,0,0,0,,So, please, just calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.30,0:15:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be back soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.56,0:15:08.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, but I am perfectly calm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.54,0:15:12.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The only one who isn't\Ncalm here, 73, 79, is you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.22,0:15:15.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you going to abandon me?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.14,0:15:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be back right away, Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.72,0:15:22.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Pale Snake, take a disc from\Nmy collection and hand it to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.44,0:15:29.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't control all of them, but\NI can choose one to enact my will!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.66,0:15:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Explode after flying 10 meters!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.16,0:15:34.70,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a direct order!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.34,0:15:48.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, my eyes, help me, please\Ncall somebody, father.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.82,0:15:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I need medical attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.88,0:15:57.22,Default,,0,0,0,,83, 89, 97, if you want\Nme, I'm right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.12,0:15:59.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Just open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.78,0:16:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You must know if I'm able to\Nleave here and call for help,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.42,0:16:04.36,Default,,0,0,0,,you can get treatment right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.70,0:16:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,That is what you were thinking, is it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.08,0:16:11.85,Default,,0,0,0,,If so, why would you not make it a priority\Nto move in the direction of my voice?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.42,0:16:17.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.58,0:16:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The disc that contains\NShotaro Kujo, Star Platinum.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.86,0:16:27.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly what should I do about it now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.14,0:16:30.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I took care of Jolene, but I can't\Njust leave her in the courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.40,0:16:32.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Did the gate finally open?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.52,0:16:33.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Please take me with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.66,0:16:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Who? Father? Hello? Father? Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.50,0:16:41.74,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.82,0:16:44.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't hold back the poison anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.46,0:16:45.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And I dropped the disc.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.32,0:16:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't even know where it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.22,0:17:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,The rain has stopped but where is
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.74,0:17:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene Kujo's lifeless body. If I find her
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.62,0:17:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I should find the disc I was frightened\Nthere for a moment but there's no way
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.86,0:17:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,frogs can defeat a snake search for it\Npalesnake's range of movement is barely
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.66,0:17:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,20 meters at best I'm running a huge\Nrisk by even being here if someone sees?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.12,0:17:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,tells me all bets are off,\Nbut there's no other way.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.28,0:17:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,The soul of a deceased criminal\Nreturns to Earth in the form of a frog
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.38,0:17:46.10,Default,,0,0,0,,in the name of trying to bring its\Ncompanions to the land of the dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.18,0:17:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I have heard that in the East there\Nare stories of a similar nature,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.88,0:17:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,but this horror is truly the\Npersonification of that proverb.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.96,0:17:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Nonetheless, the disk I seek\Nmust be around here somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.54,0:17:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, Pale Snake.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.66,0:18:03.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to sweep the area between where\Nyou are and the entrance to the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.92,0:18:06.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The guard may have taken it earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.14,0:18:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It should be in that direction.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.26,0:18:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, here it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.50,0:18:16.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I have retrieved the disc.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.12,0:18:18.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.34,0:18:21.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been waiting for\Nyou to find where it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.08,0:18:38.36,Default,,0,0,0,,This is so gross, they're all over\Nmy face, makes me want to throw up.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.48,0:18:42.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The poison only comes out when\Nthe frogs splatter on impact,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.66,0:18:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,so if they don't explode they're harmless.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.44,0:18:48.02,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I made a\Nnet using live frogs in
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.10,0:18:50.75,Default,,0,0,0,,order to lessen the\Nimpact of the frogs still
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.16,0:18:55.16,Default,,0,0,0,,falling, which allowed me to lay\Nin wait for you to locate the disk.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.02,0:18:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't matter!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.30,0:19:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You lost!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.78,0:19:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Accept your fate and die!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.46,0:19:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, it was already here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.38,0:19:17.22,Default,,0,0,0,,The Speedwagon Foundation's\Nmessenger wasn't human.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.30,0:19:21.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You just didn't even see that\Nit was here right on time,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.84,0:19:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,weaving through the deadly\Nrain of frogs like an angel.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.32,0:19:26.03,Default,,0,0,0,,It made it to this courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.56,0:19:28.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Savage Guardian is the\Nname of that pigeon.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.94,0:19:33.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And like all trained carrier pigeons, it\Nwill bring the disc to its rightful place.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.60,0:19:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Hail Snake!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.68,0:19:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The gun that the guard dropped\Nearlier is still over near the gate!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.80,0:19:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Blow that bird out of the sky!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.06,0:19:47.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Ugh, idiotic guard!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.58,0:19:49.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He completely emptied the clip of bullets!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.70,0:19:50.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.96,0:19:53.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I won.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.60,0:19:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't underestimate me, you insolent brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.12,0:19:58.60,Default,,0,0,0,,This changes nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.68,0:20:00.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Even with Star Platinum returned,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.72,0:20:02.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Your father would be nothing\Nmore than a broken puppet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.88,0:20:05.98,Default,,0,0,0,,He will never be able to recognize\Nyou as his own daughter again.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.06,0:20:08.04,Default,,0,0,0,,This little game is over!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.12,0:20:10.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey look, there's a guard\Nknocked out over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.02,0:20:12.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't step on the frauds.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.84,0:20:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And check the courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.75,0:20:15.26,Default,,0,0,0,,There might be someone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.14,0:20:19.54,Default,,0,0,0,,No, not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.62,0:20:21.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't faint here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.52,0:20:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,The stand user has to be nearby somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.80,0:20:27.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to find out who\NPale Snake really is.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.12,0:20:30.90,Default,,0,0,0,,And the user still has\Nmy father's memory disk.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.00,0:20:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Now's the best chance I'm gonna\Nget to discover who they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.10,0:20:37.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.01,0:20:39.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Look outside the window!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.46,0:20:41.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh my god! Unbelievable!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.64,0:20:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a bloody miracle!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.56,0:20:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,But who's gonna clean up this mess?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.78,0:20:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing has changed at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.42,0:20:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The only reason I stole Star\NPlatinum in the first place was
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.04,0:20:54.76,Default,,0,0,0,,to defeat Jotaro Kujo and avenge\Nthe death of my best friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.44,0:20:59.91,Default,,0,0,0,,What matters most is the memory disk,\Nand it still remains in my possession.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.10,0:21:01.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything is going as planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.52,0:21:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The instructions on how to reach Heaven\Ncan only be found in Jotaro's memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.42,0:21:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,An abnormal occurrence\Nwhere frogs rained down
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.94,0:21:22.53,Default,,0,0,0,,from the sky solely in\Nthe prison courtyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.16,0:21:28.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Through the chaos of\Nthis unexplainable event,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.30,0:21:31.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene's attempt at\Nescaping went unquestioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.74,0:21:35.68,Default,,0,0,0,,And thanks to a feathered friend,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.88,0:21:38.14,Default,,0,0,0,,the Speedwagon Foundation\Nobtained the disc
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.22,0:21:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,which contains Jotaro\NKujo's Star Platinum.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.28,0:21:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,However, without the memory disc, Jotaro's\Nmind and soul will never be restored.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.70,0:22:02.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Although you think I cope,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.16,0:22:07.50,Default,,0,0,0,,my head is filled with hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.58,0:22:12.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Of some place.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.20,0:22:15.78,Default,,0,0,0,,other than here?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.50,0:22:22.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Although you think I smile
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.80,0:22:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Inside and all the while
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.04,0:22:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm wondering about my destiny.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.96,0:22:39.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm thinking
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.96,0:22:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,about all the
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.66,0:22:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,things I'd like
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.52,0:22:56.44,Default,,0,0,0,,to do in my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.30,0:23:01.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a dreamer.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.80,0:23:06.48,Default,,0,0,0,,A distant dreamer.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.70,0:23:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Dreaming for all?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.44,0:23:16.52,Default,,0,0,0,,From today!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.86,0:23:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sports Maximum.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.12,0:23:25.90,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the bone that I\Nwant to ask you about.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.22,0:23:28.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Using your unique abilities,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.90,0:23:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,there is something I\Nwould like to try really
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.18,0:23:35.80,Default,,0,0,0,,does that belong to a\Nhuman whose bone is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.88,0:23:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,That answer is none of your business.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.78,0:23:40.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's just say it belongs\Nto an old friend of mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.56,0:23:43.20,Default,,0,0,0,,The bone of my dear friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.28,0:23:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,The great deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.90,0:23:56.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.74,0:24:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
